<title>USA: Q2 U.S. mortgage delinquencies 4.35 pct--MBA.</title>
<headline>Q2 U.S. mortgage delinquencies 4.35 pct--MBA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mortgage delinquencies in the second quarter declined to a seasonally adjusted 4.35 percent versus 4.46 percent the previous quarter, the Mortgage Bankers Association of America (MBA) said Thursday.</p>
<p>The new rate for one- to four-unit homes was also down from the recent high of 4.48 percent in the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Delinquency rates may have peaked for this economic cycle,&quot; said Warren Lasko, the association's executive vice president, in a statement.</p>
